# ETPL Beginner's Guide
## Learning to Code in the Exception Theory Programming Language

---

> **ETPL** is a language whose structure mirrors the structure of reality itself. Every program you write is an expression of the same three primitives that constitute existence: **Points (P)**, **Descriptors (D)**, and **Traversers (T)**. You are not learning syntax grafted onto an ad-hoc history of committee decisions. You are learning a language built from a single, coherent ontological foundation — and every feature of the language traces back to that foundation without exception.
>
> ETPL compiles to native machine code and runs directly on bare metal. There is no virtual machine, no garbage collector, no interpreter overhead, no runtime environment sitting between your program and the hardware. What you write is what runs.

---

