## The Master Equation — Revisited

You have now read this guide. Every concept in it — from the simplest Point declaration to the Incoherence framework to the mandatory loop bound — traces back to one equation:

```
P ∘ D ∘ T = E
```

**P** — declare your substrates. Know what exists.\
**D** — define your constraints. Know what transforms it.\
**T** — navigate your decisions. Know what moves through it.\
**E** — arrive at the grounded result. Know what is actual.

When your program is coherent — when no two Descriptors applied to the same substrate contradict each other, when every Traverser has a finite Descriptor to navigate, when T always reaches P through D — there are no errors.

Not because errors are caught. Because the conditions for them do not exist.

That is what it means to write in ETPL.

